WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.840
Install SpecWeave and plan your first increment.

2
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.113
Install the CLI from npm

3
00:00:08.113 --> 00:00:11.419
with npm i -g specweave.

4
00:00:11.419 --> 00:00:14.421
It needs Node 20.12 or later.

5
00:00:14.421 --> 00:00:18.670
specweave --version prints 3.1.0.

6
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.528
In your repo, run specweave init with the Claude Code adapter.

7
00:00:23.528 --> 00:00:26.800
It writes CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md,

8
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.840
installs six SpecWeave skills,

9
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.820
and keeps its settings in .specweave/config.json.

10
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.761
Now plan the work. Give specweave create-increment a title.

11
00:00:37.761 --> 00:00:41.990
It makes the folder 0001-personal-greeting,

12
00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.330
with a spec.md to fill in.

13
00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:49.020
Step one is Decide. At the default level, critical,

14
00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.226
your agent asks only the decisions that are yours,

15
00:00:52.226 --> 00:00:54.880
one at a time with a recommended answer.

16
00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.605
Then fill in spec.md,

17
00:00:57.605 --> 00:01:00.922
yourself or with the sw-increment skill:

18
00:01:00.922 --> 00:01:05.190
the problem, and numbered acceptance criteria that a test can check.

19
00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:10.581
Decisions records what was asked, what was defaulted, and what is open.

20
00:01:10.581 --> 00:01:14.640
Each task names its acceptance criterion, its files,

21
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.580
and the test that proves it.

22
00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.722
Commit the plan, then run specweave pickup.

23
00:01:19.722 --> 00:01:23.590
It shows the increment, the next task, T-01,

24
00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:27.150
with its acceptance criterion, files and test,

25
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.060
and the command that claims it.

26
00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.830
Next, claim T-01

27
00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:35.510
and prove it with task done --run.
